[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0
diagnosis_text:
The failure is on the access interface of leaf_router_0_0, not on pc_0_0’s NIC or cabling. On pc_0_0, eth0 is UP/LOWER_UP with link detected (ethtool shows link: yes), correct IP 10.0.0.2/24 and default via 10.0.0.1, but it receives no frames (RX 0) and ARP to 10.0.0.1 times out. On the leaf side, interface eth2 (the host-facing port) is down: “ip link” shows state DOWN with no UP/RUNNING flags, and ethtool reports “Link detected: no.” The router still has 10.0.0.1/24 configured on eth2, but because the interface is down, L2 neighbor discovery fails and the host gets “Destination Host Unreachable.”

The fabric core is otherwise healthy: leaf_router_0_0 has BGP-learned reachability for 10.0.1.0/24 via its spine links, and leaf_router_0_1’s host-facing eth2 toward pc_0_1 is UP with link detected yes. This localizes the outage to leaf_router_0_0’s eth2 only.

Root cause: leaf_router_0_0’s access interface eth2 toward pc_0_0 is administratively/operationally down, isolating the host.

Corrective fix: Do not swap the workstation NIC/cable. Bring up the leaf access port. On leaf_router_0_0, run “ip link set dev eth2 up” (or restart the device to reinitialize interfaces). If you prefer a restart: restart leaf_router_0_0; that will restore the host-facing interface and pc_0_0’s connectivity.
=== END ===